  "description": "Warm-weather drinks made with pineapple are often one-note, and that note is sweet. But this cocktail is mellow, earthy, tart, and fruity.",
  "notes": "Notes: To make pineapple juice from scratch without a juicer, muddle or blend 3/4 cup of cubed peeled fresh pineapple, then strain through a fine-mesh strainer. This cocktail was designed using Calyx Gin, which is dry, crisp, and loaded with spice and grapefruit. If you can't find the Calyx, choose a bold, juniper-heavy London Dry, not a softer, New Western–style gin.",
